  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(|a|=-a\\) means that the absolute value of \\(a\\) equals its additive inverse. This holds only when \\(a\\leq0\\), so \\(a\\) is nonpositive (note that \\(a=0\\) also satisfies the condition).",
